  "result": "Done. All 8 tests pass (5 existing plus the 3 new ones in tests/test_t2.py).\n\n**What changed in `bus/eventbus.py`:**\n\n- **Wildcard subscriptions.** A new `_matching_handlers` helper collects exact-topic handlers first, then handlers for every wildcard prefix of the topic, most specific first. So `orders.*` matches `orders.created` and also `orders.a.b`, and `a.b.*` runs before `a.*` for topic `a.b.c`. The dispatch loop in `flush` now uses this helper instead of an exact-only lookup.\n- **`once(topic, handler)`.** Registers a wrapper through `subscribe` that unsubscribes itself before delegating to the handler, and returns the unsubscribe function like `subscribe` does. Because each event snapshots its handler list, a second queued event for the same topic no longer sees the removed handler. It works with wildcard topics too.\n- **Module docstring** updated to describe wildcard matching order and `once`.\n\nNo test files or public interface were modified. Changes are uncommitted in the working tree.",
